t Donald Trump  should have been times Person of the  Year and we also know that Donald Trump  at least at one point was displaying  these fake Person of the Year covers at  some of his properties at some of his  golf clubs and and apparently those may  have since been taken down fake right  fake Time magazine covers were on the  wall at some of Donald Trump's golf  course offices why lie about this what  is the point of lying about something so  trivial and something that is  demonstrably falsifiable I mean this is  a provably false claim and there are  sort of two explanations right one  explanation is this is all part of  Trump's 4d chess that he's playing it's  some kind of brilliant political  strategy so complex that we can't  understand it or it might just be more  evidence that Donald Trump is a  pathological liar with serious  personality disorders I lean towards the  latter on this one and I got a couple of  emails from people saying David  why didn't Time magazine just say Trump  is lying why did they use the language  that they used in the tweet this is  actually something a lot of people in  the audience have asked me more  generally why aren't media outlets more  frequently just straight up saying  Donald Trump is lying as opposed to  saying that he is misstating and this is  actually an interesting thing corporate  media typically avoids using the word  liar because it does have the potential  to create a legal problem for them  because when you're saying someone lied  you're making an implication about  intent there and you might not  necessarily be able to prove that so  saying that something is a misstatement  or not a reflection of reality or  whatever that is more legally ironclad  than saying that someone lied and that's  why I wouldn't expect corporate media to  start using that term particularly when  Trump has been very clear that he wants  to make it easier to sue media outlets  so don't expect the term liar to be used  anytime soon although